00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.280
but I've already covered Re:Zero extensively in my review and parody of it

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:18.600
so instead of repeating myself, let me take this time to talk about my actual favorite show of the season.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.880
In a time when the only way shonen battle series

00:07:22.889 --> 00:07:25.140
would get notice will be by adding a darker twist to it

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.820
or subverting the tropes in a clever way

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.320
or by being JoJo's

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.900
it was nice to see a shonen that just went back to its roots and doing it really fucking well

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:38.039
Boku no Hero Academia was nothing more than a celebration of the tropes you've seen many times before

00:07:38.039 --> 00:07:39.379
but refined to a T(?)

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.940
demonstrating to us that you don't always need to do something overly original off the cuff(?)

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.340
if you just get the basics absolutely right

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.459
Deku's pure childlike desire to become a hero

00:07:47.459 --> 00:07:51.339
make him incredibly sympathetic to any person who's cheered for the heroes as a kid

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:54.260
and All Might was one of the most likable characters I've seen in anime,

00:07:54.269 --> 00:07:59.560
humanizing the charismatic mentor type in a way that you looked up to him yet related to him at the same time

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.180
the charm of the series made it incredibly easy to get behind the characters and moments

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.320
no matter how cheesy or predictable they were,

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.960
giving you back your gitty(?) childhood excitement of the best of times

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.660
so i highly recommend it for any shonen fans or if you're just looking for something fun

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.220
also not to mention next season we're getting a tournament arc

